# Skript command starter (see 14)

```applescript
command /warp <text=text> [<text=text>]:
  description: Travel to a named warp.
  usage: /warp <create|delete|go|list> ...
  aliases: warps
  permission: plugin.warp.base
  permission message: You do not have permission to do that.
  executable by: players
  trigger:
    if arg-1 is "go":
      if arg-2 is not set:
        send mini message "<red>Usage: /warp go <name></red>" to player
        stop
      # domain lookup, NOT script-internals in command names
      teleport player to warp arg-2
    else if arg-1 is "list":
      send mini message "<aqua>Warps:</aqua> %warps%" to player
    else:
      send mini message "<red>Usage: /warp <create|delete|go|list> ...</red>" to player
```

Rules: parser failures (missing args) vs domain failures (unknown warp) produce different messages; player-only vs console is declared, not assumed; tab completion where the runtime supports it; search all `.sk` callers before renaming (50).
